  "110": {
    "inputs": {
      "prompt": "Transform the provided anime image into a physically realistic live-action photograph.\n\nReconstruct the entire scene as if it had been photographed in the real world with a professional full-frame camera. Preserve exactly the original character’s identity, recognizable facial structure, hairstyle, hair length, hair color, eye color, body proportions, clothing design, accessories, pose, hand placement, facial expression, gaze direction, camera angle, framing, composition, environment, object positions and narrative context.\n\nTranslate every stylized anime element into a believable real-world equivalent:\n\n- Reconstruct the face with realistic human anatomy, natural facial proportions, authentic bone structure and subtle facial asymmetry.\n- Preserve the distinctive shape of the eyes, eyebrows, nose, lips, jawline and hairstyle without making the person generic.\n- Convert illustrated skin into natural human skin with pores, fine facial hairs, subtle imperfections, realistic subsurface scattering and natural tonal variation.\n- Convert illustrated hair into individually visible hair strands with realistic density, roots, flyaway hairs, volume and physically plausible highlights.\n- Reconstruct the eyes with realistic sclera, iris texture, corneal reflections, tear line and natural moisture.\n- Convert the clothing into real fabric with accurate stitching, seams, folds, thickness, tension, texture and material response.\n- Rebuild the environment using physically plausible materials, depth, perspective, contact shadows and realistic reflections.\n- Preserve the original lighting direction and atmosphere, but convert them into physically accurate cinematic photographic lighting.\n- Use realistic depth of field, natural lens behavior, coherent perspective and believable exposure.\n\nThe result must look like an authentic live-action cinematic photograph of a real person in a real location, not a digital painting, illustration, CGI render, cosplay photograph or obvious AI-generated image.\n\nPreserve the original aspect ratio and composition. Do not add, remove, replace or redesign any character, object, accessory, garment or environmental element.",
